pendencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.4.1.stable.official [49a5bc7b6]\n\nTested with editor setting `run/platforms/linuxbsd/prefer_wayland` enabled as well as when disabled.\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable - Fedora Linux 42 (Workstation Edition) on Wayland - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility)\n\n### Issue description\n\nNon-embedded sub-windows, don't receive touch input events when `input_devices/pointing/emulate_touch_from_mouse` is set to `true` in the project settings.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. In Project Settings:\n   - Check `input_devices/pointing/emulate_touch_from_mouse`\n   - Uncheck `display/window/subwindows/embed_subwindows`\n1. Create a script that tests received input events for touch. For example:\n    ```gdscript\n    # test.gd\n    extends Node\n    func _input(event: InputEvent) -> void:\n\t    if event is InputEventScreenTouch or event is InputEventMouseButton:\n\t        print(event.as_text())\n    ```\n1. Create an empty scene, add a `Window` Node, and attach the script.\n1. When running the scene and clicking inside of the sub-window, you should see in the output log that only mouse events are received.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[touch_input_test_subwindow_godot-4-4-1.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22099724/touch_input_test_subwindow_godot-4-4-1.zip) (1.6 kB)","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_u